<!-- The N.D.N.Y. Bankruptcy motion brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in
     the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman: the house standard; was EB Garamond) at 12 pt (LBR
     9004-1(a)(1)(A): minimum 12-point; size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double:
     LBR 9004-1(a)(1)(B), double-spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent; headings on the body pitch, 24 pt above;
     caption, counsel, block quotations (LBR 9004-1(a)(1)(B)) and signature in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins (LBR
     9004-1(a)(2)(A), (C)) and a centered page number on every page (LBR 9004-1(a)(2)(B)), its line 36.75 pt above the
     page foot (735 twips: where typst sets it, footer-descent 30 %). docx/nynb-motion-brief.lua writes every
     paragraph's own spacing. pandoc reads the sample without fancy lists, so a paragraph opening "A." or "(a)" stays a
     paragraph, as typst reads it. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
